                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc82f8e6-33b8-39cf-92e3-4a29bbbc6fd0",
                                        "entry_id": "99a5b7c4-3708-3f77-8b5c-310a91c7682a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An appliance or utensil for cooking food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                        "entry_id": "99a5b7c4-3708-3f77-8b5c-310a91c7682a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who cooks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edc0b434-0b8e-4a4d-92d7-6f967961d1e0",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "[…] I am a true † cooker of men, that is to ſay, I not only dreſs and prepare ſuch vile eatables as theſe, but that green creature, called man, I kill, and cut in pieces, aye, and devour him too, heart and all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdc81988-d99a-47fa-821b-f528521f742b",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "And, if we may believe the tale, / Her canny hand will ſcarcely fail, / Whate’er ſhe tries, to help or heal, / She’ll ſeldom blunder; / If ſhe be cooker of the kail, / She’ll gar us wonder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edd0fc09-4f80-48c1-b7d4-1d8f631e829e",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "She was, in sooth, a most delicious cooker of delicious tit-bits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ea606c2-4a0e-4e0b-b7c6-fcb4597261c7",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "“A most excellent cooker of eggs, is Mrs. J.,” I said to my companion (silent companions are often the best of company); “most excellent. Few people can be relied upon to always cook one’s eggs properly, but Mrs. J. is one of the few.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "486c8b3e-8491-4cab-9f4b-45283fa0139b",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "As the hon. Provincial Treasurer knows, he is the greatest cooker of the books, and when he leaves here he can get a job as a chef at the King Edward hotel—"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4095fc2b-7e03-418d-89d5-8397f1e6e8a7",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "“[…] I know how to cook a steak, if you don’t.” “I am, sir, one of the world’s great cookers of steak,” Charley said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2378be7-b446-4fca-be4c-e13e75cc41e6",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "The question was asked by a guy named Ernie, who lives on the South Side and believes he is the greatest cooker of ribs in the land. […] Besides the admiration and envy of the nation’s rib cookers, the winner will receive a trophy and a special license plate indicating big achievement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d938e17b-a9f7-49f7-990d-eb0efe783b97",
                                                "sense_id": "97aaf469-d964-3231-ab36-590f669cdfb2",
                                                "text": "Duke Ellington, the royal man of jazz, claimed he was the “world’s greatest cooker of eggs” and also swore by the stimulating nature of caviar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7a6f474-3520-3d46-a0db-75bb3c9164a4",
                                        "entry_id": "99a5b7c4-3708-3f77-8b5c-310a91c7682a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of cooking apple."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43046d86-7bc7-43bc-8595-789c08375bd6",
                                                "sense_id": "e7a6f474-3520-3d46-a0db-75bb3c9164a4",
                                                "text": "For the British market, apples are classed as early, mid-season, or late, and subdivided into eaters or cookers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1fd91fc3-cffe-3919-89bd-38ca58f57013",
                                        "entry_id": "99a5b7c4-3708-3f77-8b5c-310a91c7682a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who makes or uses illicit drugs, especially methamphetamine or cannabis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31f61a21-05c5-335b-a74e-133249f7bcb0",
                                        "entry_id": "99a5b7c4-3708-3f77-8b5c-310a91c7682a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The container in which recreational drugs are prepared."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
